question.:question/worked-solution:
Use the **product rule**: $\nabla(fg)=g\nabla f+f\nabla g$. Multiply each gradient by the other scalar function.

First find the partial derivatives, holding other coordinates constant:

$$
\begin{aligned}
f_{x}&=4 x y \\ g_{x}&=- 2 e^{- 2 x - 2 y^{2}} \\ f_{y}&=2 x^{2} \\ g_{y}&=- 4 y e^{- 2 x - 2 y^{2}}
\end{aligned}
$$

Now collect each component:

$$
\begin{aligned}
(\nabla(fg))_{x}&=g f_{x}+f g_{x} \\ &=(e^{- 2 x - 2 y^{2}})(4 x y) \\ &\quad+(2 x^{2} y)(- 2 e^{- 2 x - 2 y^{2}}) \\ &=4 x y e^{- 2 x - 2 y^{2}} \\ &\quad+(- 4 x^{2} y e^{- 2 x - 2 y^{2}}) \\ &=4 x y \left(1 - x\right) e^{- 2 x - 2 y^{2}}
\end{aligned}
$$

$$
\begin{aligned}
(\nabla(fg))_{y}&=g f_{y}+f g_{y} \\ &=(e^{- 2 x - 2 y^{2}})(2 x^{2}) \\ &\quad+(2 x^{2} y)(- 4 y e^{- 2 x - 2 y^{2}}) \\ &=2 x^{2} e^{- 2 x - 2 y^{2}} \\ &\quad+(- 8 x^{2} y^{2} e^{- 2 x - 2 y^{2}}) \\ &=2 x^{2} \left(1 - 4 y^{2}\right) e^{- 2 x - 2 y^{2}}
\end{aligned}
$$

Thus the gradient is

$$
\begin{aligned}&4 x y \left(1 - x\right) e^{- 2 x - 2 y^{2}}\mathbf i \\ &{}+2 x^{2} \left(1 - 4 y^{2}\right) e^{- 2 x - 2 y^{2}}\mathbf j\end{aligned}
$$

Collect the contributions to each coordinate separately.

