question.:question/worked-solution:
Use the **product rule**: $\nabla(fg)=g\nabla f+f\nabla g$. Multiply each gradient by the other scalar function.

Now collect each component:

$$
\begin{aligned}
(\nabla(fg))_{x}&=g f_{x}+f g_{x} \\ &=(2 x^{2} + x y)(- 2 e^{- 2 x - 2 y}) \\ &\quad+(e^{- 2 x - 2 y})(4 x + y) \\ &=- 2 x \left(2 x + y\right) e^{- 2 x - 2 y} \\ &\quad+(\left(4 x + y\right) e^{- 2 x - 2 y}) \\ &=\left(- 4 x^{2} - 2 x y + 4 x + y\right) e^{- 2 x - 2 y}
\end{aligned}
$$

$$
\begin{aligned}
