\end{aligned}
$$

Thus the gradient is

$$
\begin{aligned}&\left(- 4 x^{2} - 2 x y + 4 x + y\right) e^{- 2 x - 2 y}\mathbf i \\ &{}+x \left(- 4 x - 2 y + 1\right) e^{- 2 x - 2 y}\mathbf j\end{aligned}
$$

Collect the contributions to each coordinate separately.

