$$
\begin{aligned}
(\nabla(fg))_{z}&=g f_{z}+f g_{z} \\ &=\left(\frac{1}{x y z}\right)(- 2 x^{2} y^{3}) \\ &\quad+(- 2 x^{2} y^{3} z)\left(- \frac{1}{x y z^{2}}\right) \\ &=- \frac{2 x y^{2}}{z} \\ &\quad+\left(\frac{2 x y^{2}}{z}\right) \\ &=0
\end{aligned}
$$

Thus the gradient is

$$
- 2 y^{2}\mathbf i- 4 x y\mathbf j
$$

Collect the contributions to each coordinate separately.
